From d3d32afba91d6d16d5f954643318f3124d5e741a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tuan Pham <tuan.p83@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:41:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(deploy):=20make=20docker-compose.prod.yml?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20actually=20deployable=20(N1=E2=80=93N5)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

N1  nginx: move the production server block to nginx/prod/default.conf and
    mount only that directory. nginx/conf.d/rtms.conf (dev) referenced hosts
    `api`/`web` that did not exist in production, so nginx refused to start;
    the dev stack no longer loads a TLS block without certificates either.
N2  seed: the production admin is created from ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD
    (policy-checked, random salt, same format as PasswordService) with
    mustChangePassword=true. The previous hash used the dev salt under a new
    prefix and matched no password. Re-running the seed in production never
    overwrites an existing account.
N3  compose: one-shot `migrate` service runs `prisma migrate deploy`; `api`
    starts only after it completes successfully.
N4  compose: MinIO variables renamed to the MINIO_* names the code reads
    (MINIO_ENDPOINT, MINIO_ACCESS_KEY, MINIO_SECRET_KEY, MINIO_BUCKET_NAME,
    MINIO_USE_SSL); previously every file upload/download failed.
N5  Dockerfile: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is a build arg (default /api/v1)
    so browsers call the public origin instead of http://localhost:4000;
    web middleware uses API_INTERNAL_BASE_URL=http://api:4000/api/v1.
N6  Dockerfile: workspace manifests/packages are copied before `npm ci` so
    @rtms/permissions is linked at runtime; prisma.config.ts is included.

Also:
- api and web run as separate services with health checks instead of two
  background processes in one container.
- All secrets are required (${VAR:?}); no fallback passwords.
- postgres:16 to match development.
- nginx client_max_body_size 11m to match FILE_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES (10 MB).
- .dockerignore keeps .env, .git, node_modules, reports/ and output/ out of
  the build context and image.
- scripts/backup.sh: pg_dump -Fc via `exec -T` (no TTY), MinIO backed up from
  the named volume (the old path did not exist and errors were swallowed),
  integrity checks, SHA256SUMS, fails loudly. New scripts/restore.sh.
- .env.production.example documents every required variable.

Not verified by a Docker build in the authoring environment; validate with
`docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml --env-file .env.production up --build`.

